<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  OpenArm v2 bimanual — hand-reviewed self-collision exemptions.

  This SRDF exists ONLY to carry deliberate ACM exemptions into the MJCF
  collision lowering (`openral collision lower`, source: mjcf). The sweep can
  auto-disable a pair only when it collides in EVERY sampled pose; these pairs
  do NOT (fractions below, 2000 seeded samples over the joint limits with the
  manifest capsules + mujoco FK), yet they DO collide at the robot's rest pose,
  so checking them would E-stop the arm at home. Disabling them is therefore a
  reviewed usability judgment, not a sweep result — recorded here, the same
  explicit channel URDF robots use, instead of hand edits to the generated ACM
  block (which are unreproducible and broke the fleet lowering regression).

  Originally introduced with the 2026-06-20 capsule re-placement
  ("fix(robots): correct OpenArm collision-capsule placement + wrist/gripper
  ACM"); re-measured 2026-07-09:
    link1<->link3         collides in ~23% of poses, rest pose d=-0.0006 m
    finger_pair<->link5   collides in ~50% of poses, rest pose d=-0.051 m
    finger_pair<->link6   collides in ~57% of poses, rest pose d=-0.052 m
  The former finger_pair<->link4 exemption was REMOVED: it never collides
  (min clearance +0.021 m across 2000 poses, clear at rest) — the kernel now
  checks it.

  SAFETY (CLAUDE.md §3): every row here REDUCES what the kernel checks and
  needs safety-WG sign-off to change.
-->
<robot name="openarm">
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_link1" link2="openarm_left_link3" reason="Rest-pose contact (d=-0.0006 m at qpos0) under the conservative capsules; not always-colliding (23%)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_link1" link2="openarm_right_link3" reason="Rest-pose contact (d=-0.0006 m at qpos0) under the conservative capsules; not always-colliding (23%)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_finger_pair" link2="openarm_left_link5" reason="Folded gripper rests beside the forearm (d=-0.051 m at qpos0); not always-colliding (50%)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_finger_pair" link2="openarm_right_link5" reason="Folded gripper rests beside the forearm (d=-0.051 m at qpos0); not always-colliding (49%)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_finger_pair" link2="openarm_left_link6" reason="Folded gripper rests beside the wrist (d=-0.052 m at qpos0); not always-colliding (57%)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_finger_pair" link2="openarm_right_link6" reason="Folded gripper rests beside the wrist (d=-0.052 m at qpos0); not always-colliding (56%)."/>
</robot>
